//
// The fused DECODER's re-execution gate. `[2026-08-19]` This pins the class
// of defect that survived every single-dispatch check in the suite: the
// causal mha's Q-block base lived in uninitialized L1 behind a boot flag and
// never wrapped, so the fused decoder's first dispatch was 12/12 boundaries
// clean while every later one computed UNMASKED attention with q/k/v still
// clean (devq 382-384). The fix wraps the counter modulo the execution's
// total Q blocks (attn_npu2*.py); this gate dispatches ONE prepared stitch
// TWICE and requires both dispatches clean plus a causal correlation on the
// second -- reverting the wrap flips the second dispatch's verdict line, so
// the gate is red exactly on the defect. The encoder fused gate
// (run_npu2_fused_peano) cannot see any of this: its attention is
// non-causal, so the counter code is never emitted there.
//
// NPU serialization lives one layer down (KernelCache takes /tmp/npu.lock,
// the same inode lit.cfg.py's NPU substitution takes); taking the outer lock
// here would deadlock, same note as the other device gates in this suite.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_fused_decoder_reexec
// RUN: cd test_npu2_fused_decoder_reexec
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-fused-decoder-reexec PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
//
// Both dispatches clean, the second causally correlated, and the driver's
// own verdict last -- three independent clauses, so a partial failure names
// the dispatch it happened on.
// CHECK: [reexec] dispatch 1: 12/12 boundaries clean
// CHECK: [reexec] dispatch 2: 12/12 boundaries clean
// CHECK: [reexec] dispatch 2 attn_context corr vs causal reference: {{(0\.99[0-9][0-9]|1\.0000)}}
// CHECK: [reexec] PASS
